{"id":"van-buren-1916","title":"The Van Buren sisters cross America","who":"Augusta & Adeline Van Buren","when":"1916","vehicle":"Two Indian Power Plus motorcycles","kind":"moto","color":"#7c3aed","summary":"Two sisters, each on her own 1,000 cc Indian, ride 5,500 miles in 60 days from Brooklyn to Los Angeles to prove women could serve as military dispatch riders: the first women to cross the US on solo motorcycles. Arrested for wearing men's clothes, they were also the first women to drive up Pikes Peak; the army still turned them down.","sources":[{"label":"History Today: the first women to cross the US on solo motorcycles","url":"https://www.historytoday.com/archive/months-past/first-women-cross-us-solo-motorcycles"},{"label":"Expedition Portal: the Van Buren sisters' 1916 ride","url":"https://expeditionportal.com/pioneers-of-moto-history-the-van-buren-sisters-1916-ride-across-america/"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Van Buren sisters","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Van_Buren_sisters"}],"approximate":"Places named in accounts of the ride; the roads are drawn as today's, only approximately.","km":5375,"bbox":[-118.2423,32.5365,-73.9446,41.9008],"stops":[{"name":"Sheepshead Bay","place":"Sheepshead Bay, Brooklyn","at":[40.5912,-73.9446],"date":"4 Jul 1916","text":"The start from the Brooklyn race track on Independence Day.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Sheepshead_Bay_footbridge_North_jeh.JPG/500px-Sheepshead_Bay_footbridge_North_jeh.JPG","page":"Sheepshead Bay, Brooklyn","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sheepshead_Bay_footbridge_North_jeh.JPG","credit":"Jim.henderson","license":"Public domain"}},{"name":"Chicago","place":"Chicago, Illinois","at":[41.8756,-87.6244],"text":"West across the Midwest in rain and mud.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Chicago_River_ferry_b.jpg/500px-Chicago_River_ferry_b.jpg","page":"Chicago","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chicago_River_ferry_b.jpg","credit":"File:Chicago River ferry.jpg: John Picken derivative work: Georgfotoart","license":"CC BY 2.0"}},{"name":"Pikes Peak","place":"Pikes Peak, Colorado","at":[38.8404,-105.044],"text":"The first women to reach the summit by motor vehicle.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Beautiful_Image_of_Pikes_Peak_%28IMG_0136%29.jpg/500px-Beautiful_Image_of_Pikes_Peak_%28IMG_0136%29.jpg","page":"Pikes Peak","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Beautiful_Image_of_Pikes_Peak_%28IMG_0136%29.jpg","credit":"Tokeamour","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Salt Lake City","place":"Salt Lake City, Utah","at":[40.7596,-111.8868],"text":"Lost in the desert to the west, out of water, saved by a prospector.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/SLC_Skyline_2024.jpg/500px-SLC_Skyline_2024.jpg","page":"Salt Lake City","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SLC_Skyline_2024.jpg","credit":"Invictus323","license":"CC BY 4.0"}},{"name":"Los Angeles","place":"Los Angeles, California","at":[34.0537,-118.2428],"date":"8 Sep 1916","text":"5,500 miles in 60 days.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Hollywood_sign_%288485145044%29.jpg/500px-Hollywood_sign_%288485145044%29.jpg","page":"Los Angeles","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hollywood_sign_%288485145044%29.jpg","credit":"Gnaphron","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0"}},{"name":"Tijuana","place":"Tijuana, Mexico","at":[32.5365,-117.0371],"text":"A last ride over the border to finish.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Templo_Tijuana_Mexico_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Templo_Tijuana_Mexico_%28cropped%29.jpg","page":"Tijuana","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Templo_Tijuana_Mexico_%28cropped%29.jpg","credit":"Isai Armenta","license":"CC BY 4.0"}}],"legs":[{"by":"ride","km":1289,"line":[[40.5912,-73.9446],[40.692,-74.0119]